  "title": "EEG Motor Movement/Imagery Dataset",
  "description": "A collection of over 1500 one- and two-minute 64-channel EEG recordings from 109 volunteers performing motor execution and motor imagery tasks. Participants completed baseline runs (eyes open and eyes closed) and runs involving opening and closing the left or right fist, or both fists or both feet, either actually or in imagination. The data were recorded with the BCI2000 system and are provided in BIDS format with curated metadata.",
  "methods_description": "64-channel EEG was recorded with the BCI2000 system. Each subject completed 14 runs: two one-minute baseline runs (eyes open, eyes closed) and three two-minute runs for each of four tasks (real or imagined fist movement on the left or right, and real or imagined movement of both fists or both feet), cued by on-screen targets.",
